ason for this topology.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"Q1 | Q_PMOS_GSD | Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23 | Device:Q_PMOS_GSD | P-MOSFET transistor, gate/source/drain | LCSC=C347476, MPN=AO3401A\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"+5V [High Power] : ... Q1.2(S,passive)\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"USBC_VBUS_IN [High Power] : J3.A4(VBUS,passive) ... Q1.3(D,passive) R11.1(passive) R64.2(2,passive) U25.5(VBUS,passive) U6.1(VIN,power_in)\"}, {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"LTC4412 controller and p-ch mosfet. need reverse current protection mostly\"}], \"impact\": \"Reverse-current or back-feed protection on the USB input path may not work. Power could flow from +5V into the USB-C VBUS line, or the input path may not provide the intended OR-ing behaviour.\", \"confidence\": 0.35}, {\"category\": \"bridged_nets\", \"components\": [\"D30\", \"R60\"], \"pins\": [\"D30.4\", \"D30.2\", \"R60.1\", \"R60.2\"], \"nets\": [\"ESTOP_OUT\", \"Net-(D30-K2)\"], \"observed\": \"The second LED of dual LED D30 has its anode A2 (pin 4) on ESTOP_OUT. Its cathode K2 (pin 2) goes through R60 to the same ESTOP_OUT net, so both terminals of that LED sit on one node and it is shorted.\", \"expected\": \"The LED cathode should return through R60 to a different node, such as ground, as R59 does for the K1 channel. Only then does the LED light when ESTOP_OUT changes state.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"ESTOP_OUT : D30.4(A2,input) J13.6(Pin_6,passive) J2.6(Pin_6,passive) R60.2(passive) U36.4(Y,output)\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"Net-(D30-K2) : D30.2(K2,input) R60.1(passive)\"}, {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R60 Net-_D30-K2_ ESTOP_OUT 130\"}], \"impact\": \"The E-stop status LED channel tied to ESTOP_OUT cannot illuminate. R60 is also pointless as a current limit, so the indicator for the e-stop output is lost.\", \"confidence\": 0.3}], \"summary\": \"The strongest evidence is that R62 is labelled 10 ohms bu